  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "While Nastya secretly devours a piece of sausage in the storage room, Max and Ilya begin sabotaging each other's orders in the dining room to win the tip bet.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Ешь! Ненасытный.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Вот конфетка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Значит, по поводу вырезки.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она должна быть, во-первых, свежей.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Как минимум.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Ягнёнка забираем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Так, почему здесь остывает? Забираем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Приятного аппетита!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Ну что это?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Видимо, ягнёнок был очень вкусный, и повар не удержался.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Давайте я сейчас всё переделаю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Простите! Ну, ты напросился.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Ешь! Ненасытный.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Eat! Insatiable.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'eat' before landing on 'insatiable'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Вот конфетка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Here is a piece of candy.' Nastya brings out the contrast between 'here' and 'piece of candy' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Значит, по поводу вырезки.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'So, regarding the tenderloin.' Max anchors the line on 'so', while 'tenderloin' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она должна быть, во-первых, свежей.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'First of all, it must be fresh.' The grammar packs 'she' and 'fresh' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Как минимум.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'At a minimum.' The meaning hinges on 'how' working together with 'minimum' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Ягнёнка забираем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Picking up the lamb.' In Russian, the idea of 'lamb' flows naturally into 'we are taking' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Так, почему здесь остывает? Забираем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Right, why is it getting cold here? Taking it.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'so' and finishing on 'we are taking'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Приятного аппетита!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Bon appetit!' Notice how Russian expresses 'pleasant' and 'appetite' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Ну что это?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well, what is this?' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'come on' and finishing on 'this'. Max answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Видимо, ягнёнок был очень вкусный, и повар не удержался.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Apparently, the lamb was very delicious, and the cook couldn't resist.' Max brings out the contrast between 'apparently' and 'lamb' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Давайте я сейчас всё переделаю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Let me redo everything right now.' Max anchors the line on 'let's', while 'will redo' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Простите! Ну, ты напросился.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Forgive me! Well, you asked for it.' The grammar packs 'forgive' and 'asked for it' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
